  "details": "And it looks like you're multiplying something with something when you shouldn't. In addition, some areas are transparent, which is possibly a shared issue with [https://feedback.vrchat.com/bug-reports/p/turning-of-the-environment-in-the-camera-will-also-make-your-avatar-transparent]\n\nReproduction (any enviro, any shader with fwdadd support):\n\n1. Make sure both the avatar and the light source are in clipspace and neither gets culled (duh)\n\n2. Disable environment layer in masks section\n\nAttached is the example of this issue with and without lights affecting the model.\n\nI don't know what you did, but additive pass is very simple: just add each FWDADD to FWDBASE. All shadowing is done in fragment shader, not in your compositor.",
